From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: ask the title's rules whether it runs a new program itself

Alpha 7 runs a library game in the title by default ("Run inside MihawkOS"):
its page tables are then the title's, whose own container is twice the
helpers' on the standard PS5 (16,384 against 8,192). A program that holds the
title's one place but is no game, such as a launcher that starts the game and
exits, would end the session under the game it started. So the choice is
made by what the program is, as well as where it lives and what it is named:
spawn_process now asks pw_ps5_title_route (wine/ps5/pw_wine_process.c) with
the image's Unix path, its machine and its Windows path. The PS5 code applies
the path and name rules and the per-game lists (wine/ps5/pw_wine_title_game.h)
and reads the image's import and delay-import tables, and one level deeper
the DLLs it imports from its own folder (wine/ps5/pw_wine_pe_imports.h). Only
a 64-bit program that reaches a graphics API, and is no browser shell and no
.NET program, gets PW_CHILD_GRAPHICS, and a Chromium-based game's main process
(told by its folder, with the command line for its own --type= processes). Every library program's route is logged
with its reason. NtCreateUserProcess passes the Unix name it already has.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c	2026-10-31 12:47:32.957419291 -0400
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c	2026-10-31 13:21:58.700747828 -0400
@@ -402,11 +402,13 @@
  *           spawn_process
  */
 static NTSTATUS spawn_process( const RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params, int socketfd,
-                               int unixdir, char *winedebug, const struct pe_image_info *pe_info )
+                               int unixdir, char *winedebug, const struct pe_image_info *pe_info,
+                               const char *unix_name )
 {
 #ifdef __PROSPERO__
     extern int pw_ps5_spawn(int, const char *, const char *, const char *, const char *, unsigned int,
                             const char *, const char *);
+    extern unsigned int pw_ps5_title_route(const char *, unsigned short, const char *, const char *);
     UNICODE_STRING nt_cwd = {0}, true_cwd = {0};
     /* The new process's executable and command line, so the title can give it its catalog settings
      * (wine/ps5/pw_wine_process.h, the bootstrap's image and command_line); a long command line keeps its start. */
@@ -434,6 +436,10 @@
     ntdll_wcstoumbs( params->CommandLine.Buffer, params->CommandLine.Length / sizeof(WCHAR) * 3 < sizeof(command_line)
                      ? params->CommandLine.Length / sizeof(WCHAR) : (sizeof(command_line) - 1) / 3, command_line,
                      sizeof(command_line) - 1, FALSE );
+    /* Whether the title runs this program itself (wine/ps5/pw_wine_process.h, pw_ps5_title_route): by its path, its
+     * name, the per-game lists, its folder (a Chromium-based game) and the DLLs its image imports, read here from its
+     * own file; the command line tells a Chromium game's own processes from its main one. */
+    if (!flags) flags = pw_ps5_title_route( unix_name, pe_info ? pe_info->machine : 0, image, command_line );
     if (!status && pw_ps5_spawn(socketfd, getenv("WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR"), config_dir, cwd,
                                winedebug ? strchr(winedebug, '=') + 1 : NULL, flags, image, command_line))
         status = errno_to_status(errno);
@@ -992,7 +998,7 @@
 
     /* create the child process */
 
-    if ((status = spawn_process( params, socketfd[0], unixdir, winedebug, &pe_info ))) goto done;
+    if ((status = spawn_process( params, socketfd[0], unixdir, winedebug, &pe_info, unix_name ))) goto done;
 
     close( socketfd[0] );
     socketfd[0] = -1;
